# infra-os:   leap
# infra-init: systemd
# infra-path: /home/backup/.ssh
# infra-name: authorized_keys
# infra-mode: 0644
#
# zero's backup key, the one key that lets the backup user in (docs/decisions.md § zero's
# backup to three by btrfs send/receive). Root's file in root's directory, so the backup
# user cannot add another. The key opens no shell, terminal or forwarding (restrict), comes
# only from zero's tailnet address (from=), and whatever the client asks for, sshd runs the
# forced command instead, with the client's command in SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND. zero's
# mirror-backup asks for the name of the subvolume it is sending, immich or syncthing.
#
# The forced command takes that name only when it is exactly one of the two, and runs
# mirror-receive with it through `sudo -n`, which never prompts; anything else is refused
# before sudo runs. sudoers-backup allows those two invocations and nothing else, and
# mirror-receive checks the name a third time. The quotes keep the name one word that the
# shell never splits or expands.
#
# zero's two values, from server-create-backup-key.yml on 2026-11-18 (hosts/three/leap/README.md
# § Before the stick): zero's tailnet address, and /root/.ssh/mirror-backup.pub, whose
# fingerprint is SHA256:CjbPiNyKKzvTZb60xObBkwgjLWbpH6CSyq+rqXUCBI0. A new key or address
# for zero means a new line here, then a new stick or an install-system-file on three.
restrict,from="100.121.158.58",command="case \"$SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND\" in immich|syncthing) exec sudo -n /usr/local/sbin/mirror-receive \"$SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND\" ;; *) echo 'mirror-receive: refused; ask for immich or syncthing' >&2; exit 1 ;; esac" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIL+FViXrAAkhwUAvxcOInjLK0007iTUDtgZvckbhhIKa zero mirror-backup
